## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical security-first design for Azure OpenAI with code-gen, focusing on secret redaction, key vault integration, tenant isolation, and auditable logging.

## Key Concepts
- Secret management with Azure Key Vault and Managed Identity
- Request/response redaction and policy enforcement
- Data isolation per tenant and private networking
- End-to-end auditing in Purview
- Testing: redaction fuzzing and integration tests

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: redact secrets before sending to OpenAI
function redact(input, keys){
  let out = input;
  keys.forEach(k => { out = out.replace(new RegExp(k, 'g'), 'REDACTED'); });
  return out;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test drift in redaction rules across tenants?
- What data plane logs would you guard and what retention policy would you apply?

## Why This Is Asked

This tests design for guardrails, data isolation, and cost controls in Azure OpenAI deployments, a common advanced requirement for regulated customers.

## Key Concepts

- Dynamic safety policy engine
- Prompt redaction and blocking
- API Management routing
- Grounding with versioned KB (Blob + Cognitive Search)
- Per-tenant isolation (Cosmos DB) and quotas
- Telemetry and auditing (Data Lake)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal policy eval
function evaluatePrompt(prompt, policies) {
  for (const p of policies) {
    if (p.types?.some(t => prompt.includes(t))) {
      return {blocked: true, reason: p.reason}
    }
  }
  // simple redact example
  const redacted = prompt.replace(/SSN-\d{4}/g, '[REDACTED_SSN]')
  return {blocked: false, redacted}
}
```

